WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:06.020
<b>2nd Stage: Lv. 13 
You're sure to find what you want 
on the other side of the magic door</b>

00:05.560 --> 00:06.980
<b>Say, Libra...</b>

00:07.320 --> 00:09.200
<b>How far are we going to go?</b>

00:09.200 --> 00:11.440
<b>We haven't walked <i>that</i> much.</b>

00:11.440 --> 00:12.830
<b>That's Hinami!</b>

00:11.440 --> 00:15.620
<b>Besides, the real fun is in the exploring.</b>

00:12.830 --> 00:14.200
<b>Look! Mizusawa!</b>

00:16.480 --> 00:18.200
<b>And if we get caught,</b>

00:18.200 --> 00:21.360
<b>they shouldn't get too mad: you're with me.</b>

00:23.070 --> 00:25.210
<b>Oh! A dead end.</b>

00:26.010 --> 00:26.710
<b>Wait...</b>

00:27.160 --> 00:28.210
<b>there's a door.</b>

00:28.610 --> 00:30.020
<b>Will it open?</b>

00:30.020 --> 00:31.050
<b>Leave it to me.</b>

00:31.050 --> 00:32.920
<b>This is a job for a locksmith's son.</b>

00:36.510 --> 00:40.040
<b>There, in the middle of the 
castle, was a hidden garden.</b>

00:41.630 --> 00:45.400
<b>A girl named Kris was looking 
after a flying dragon.</b>

00:46.000 --> 00:47.960
<b>Non-royals were forbidden to enter.</b>

00:49.130 --> 00:50.910
<b>Wh-Who are you?</b>

00:50.910 --> 00:52.360
<b>What are you doing here?</b>

00:52.640 --> 00:55.080
<b>I'm Libra, the locksmith's son.</b>

00:55.550 --> 00:57.430
<b>And this is Alucia.</b>

00:57.430 --> 00:59.420
<b>She's the first princess of this kingdom.</b>

00:59.420 --> 01:01.900
<b>We've been friends since we were...</b>

01:04.210 --> 01:05.370
<b>Alucia?</b>

01:11.880 --> 01:13.640
<b>Alucia, what are you doing?!</b>

01:13.640 --> 01:14.880
<b>Let me go!</b>

01:15.150 --> 01:17.260
<b>If I don't break this dragon's wing,</b>

01:18.430 --> 01:20.640
<b>you'll be killed!</b>

01:23.910 --> 01:25.640
<b>Freeze, all three of you.</b>

01:25.640 --> 01:27.370
<b>Your Highness!</b>

01:27.370 --> 01:29.150
<b>Seize that man!</b>

01:29.150 --> 01:31.130
<b>His Highness's orders!</b>

01:31.130 --> 01:32.470
<b>Resistance is useless!</b>

01:32.470 --> 01:34.080
<b>Come quietly, now!</b>

01:34.080 --> 01:35.150
<b>Father...</b>

01:35.440 --> 01:37.660
<b>Libra is my younger brother—</b>

01:37.660 --> 01:41.100
<b>one of the illegitimate children you 
have scattered around the kingdom!</b>

01:42.160 --> 01:46.290
<b>Having escaped execution thanks 
to Alucia's quick thinking,</b>

01:46.570 --> 01:51.100
<b>Libra began working as a caretaker 
for both the dragon and Kris.</b>

01:51.540 --> 01:52.800
<b>Here, eat up.</b>

01:53.420 --> 01:57.170
<b>They're medicinal herbs Libra gathered 
in the valley of the flying dragons.</b>

01:59.290 --> 02:00.800
<b>Yes—it ate them!</b>

02:01.320 --> 02:03.310
<b>Now I <i>know</i> it'll be able to fly!</b>

02:05.330 --> 02:06.510
<b>It's not flying.</b>

02:07.760 --> 02:09.810
<b>D-Don't look at me like that.</b>

02:13.280 --> 02:15.570
<b>Some months passed...</b>

02:16.270 --> 02:20.620
<b>Alucia! Did you really win 
the magicraft competition?!</b>

02:20.620 --> 02:22.030
<b>That's amazing!</b>

02:22.030 --> 02:24.220
<b>I don't care how I placed.</b>

02:24.720 --> 02:26.290
<b>I just wanted this:</b>

02:26.700 --> 02:29.670
<b>a gem that increases magic power.</b>

02:29.670 --> 02:33.510
<b>This will definitely get 
that dragon off the ground!</b>

02:33.510 --> 02:35.920
<b>I really must thank you, Alucia.</b>

02:36.280 --> 02:38.600
<b>What do you want?</b>

02:38.600 --> 02:40.490
<b>What do I want...?</b>

02:43.120 --> 02:46.310
<b>I guess maybe there <i>isn't</i> anything I want.</b>

02:46.630 --> 02:47.560
<b>Huh?</b>

02:47.810 --> 02:52.860
<b>I just work hard every day, because 
I'll eventually have to be queen.</b>

02:53.110 --> 02:56.610
<b>"Just" nothing—that's really fantastic!</b>

02:56.610 --> 03:00.360
<b>I think you misunderstand me, Kris.</b>

03:00.880 --> 03:04.160
<b>I have everything. And yet...</b>

03:05.670 --> 03:07.870
<b>that's why I have nothing at all.</b>

03:14.880 --> 03:15.880
<b>Goodness!</b>

03:16.470 --> 03:18.240
<b>What a strange thing to say!</b>

03:18.240 --> 03:18.880
<b>All right:</b>

03:18.880 --> 03:20.660
<b>let's test out this gem!</b>

03:23.620 --> 03:24.830
<b>It's not flying.</b>

03:26.160 --> 03:28.140
<b>D-Don't look at me like that.</b>

03:31.120 --> 03:34.460
<b>Say, Kris... flying dragons 
can read people's minds.</b>

03:34.890 --> 03:35.970
<b>Their minds?</b>

03:36.430 --> 03:38.530
<b>They're kind, too.</b>

03:38.860 --> 03:42.030
<b>They never forget all they owe 
to the human who raises them,</b>

03:42.380 --> 03:45.570
<b>and they do all they can to 
grant that person's wishes.</b>

03:46.330 --> 03:47.530
<b>Uh-huh...</b>

03:47.790 --> 03:48.600
<b>Kris...</b>

03:49.280 --> 03:52.290
<b>you don't want to fly, do you?</b>

03:54.680 --> 03:56.740
<b>Maybe not.</b>

03:56.740 --> 04:02.010
<b>I've always <i>thought</i> I wanted 
to leave this garden.</b>

04:02.010 --> 04:03.500
<b>But now...</b>

04:05.440 --> 04:08.890
<b>The outside world had been 
something I'd yearned for.</b>

04:09.420 --> 04:12.930
<b>But... while listening 
to your stories about it,</b>

04:13.550 --> 04:15.700
<b>I found myself getting scared.</b>

04:16.150 --> 04:17.430
<b>Scared?</b>

04:17.890 --> 04:19.280
<b>After all,</b>

04:19.280 --> 04:21.930
<b>I don't know anything about 
what it's like out there,</b>

04:21.930 --> 04:25.160
<b>or what kind of people I'll find.</b>

04:25.590 --> 04:28.910
<b>Could I even find my place in that world?</b>

04:29.310 --> 04:32.410
<b>Would other people accept me?</b>

04:32.910 --> 04:34.420
<b>In that case, Kris...</b>

04:34.950 --> 04:36.420
<b>we'll go flying together!</b>

05:03.610 --> 05:04.570
<b><i>Nice.</i></b>

05:06.330 --> 05:09.070
<b>The dragon took to the air 
with no issues at all.</b>

05:09.070 --> 05:11.830
<b>Kris got permission to leave the castle,</b>

05:11.830 --> 05:15.210
<b>and Libra took her to the village.</b>

05:15.210 --> 05:16.080
<b>Wow!</b>

05:16.080 --> 05:17.500
<b>Ah! Ow ow ow...</b>

05:17.500 --> 05:19.000
<b>Are you all right?</b>

05:19.000 --> 05:20.890
<b>I'm sorry, ma'am!</b>

05:21.500 --> 05:24.510
<b>You have to pay money 
for the things you want!</b>

05:24.800 --> 05:26.630
<b>I-I'm sorry!</b>

05:26.630 --> 05:29.370
<b>You can't just <i>take</i> things—that 
makes you a thief!</b>

05:29.370 --> 05:31.060
<b>Calm down, Father.</b>

05:31.060 --> 05:34.640
<b>I apologize. This girl is unfamiliar 
with the ways of the world...</b>

05:35.760 --> 05:38.060
<b>Well, I'm against it.</b>

05:38.490 --> 05:41.920
<b>You shouldn't be working 
in the outside world.</b>

05:41.920 --> 05:42.940
<b>Why not?</b>

05:43.350 --> 05:48.000
<b>I'm sure you have other 
paths you could follow.</b>

05:48.000 --> 05:49.730
<b>Like what?!</b>

05:49.730 --> 05:52.700
<b>Do you want me to live here 
in this garden forever?</b>

05:52.980 --> 05:54.540
<b>No, that's not what I...</b>

05:54.990 --> 05:55.700
<b>Tell me...</b>

05:56.090 --> 06:01.960
<b>what's so wrong about me wanting to 
see the same world everyone else does?</b>

06:02.260 --> 06:06.160
<b>Why can't I get along with everyone?</b>

06:06.160 --> 06:10.470
<b>Why don't I know the things 
everyone takes for granted?</b>

06:10.750 --> 06:14.470
<b>Am I... an entirely different creature?</b>

06:14.840 --> 06:17.070
<b>Tell me, Libra...</b>

06:20.800 --> 06:22.940
<b>Some days later...</b>

06:23.860 --> 06:25.860
<b>Read this, Kris.</b>

06:26.110 --> 06:29.400
<b>A letter, for me? From who?</b>

06:30.420 --> 06:35.300
<b>"Thank you for the beautiful 
crown. It made me so happy."</b>

06:37.380 --> 06:39.370
<b>It's from the greengrocer's daughter.</b>

06:39.790 --> 06:44.880
<b>I gave her one of your handmade 
flower-crowns for her birthday. She loved it.</b>

06:45.260 --> 06:46.710
<b>Hence the letter.</b>

06:47.720 --> 06:50.130
<b>My floral work did that...?</b>

06:50.950 --> 06:54.140
<b>That old woman we bumped into? 
You made her happy, too.</b>

06:55.290 --> 06:57.730
<b>Don't you see?</b>

06:58.360 --> 07:02.760
<b>So many people have smiles on their 
faces because of your flowers.</b>

07:03.640 --> 07:05.810
<b>You <i>do</i> have a place in the world.</b>

07:05.810 --> 07:08.110
<b>And you're <i>not</i> a different creature.</b>

07:08.660 --> 07:09.420
<b>Uh-huh...</b>

07:10.950 --> 07:13.010
<b>So c'mon...</b>

07:14.730 --> 07:18.120
<b>Fly! On your <i>own</i> wings this time!</b>

07:30.890 --> 07:33.640
<b><i>Now for the ending.</i></b>

07:33.970 --> 07:36.390
<b>Well... here I go.</b>

07:36.640 --> 07:39.620
<b>You can always come back 
if things get too tough.</b>

07:40.090 --> 07:43.190
<b><i>I</i> won't be that soft on you.</b>

07:43.190 --> 07:46.400
<b>You go become the best 
flower artisan around—</b>

07:47.490 --> 07:51.150
<b>and you'll come home not to the garden,</b>

07:51.150 --> 07:53.500
<b>but to the castle, Kris!</b>

07:53.500 --> 07:55.410
<b>You got it!</b>

07:57.220 --> 07:58.540
<b>Yes...</b>

07:58.790 --> 08:01.190
<b>This is what I should be doing.</b>

08:02.320 --> 08:04.040
<b>At long last,</b>

08:04.480 --> 08:06.370
<b>I've found my own way to fly!</b>

08:09.870 --> 08:10.920
<b>It's over...</b>

08:11.300 --> 08:12.420
<b>and it was a success!</b>

08:15.220 --> 08:16.430
<b>Libra!</b>

08:16.430 --> 08:18.120
<b>We've got a letter from Kris!</b>

08:19.740 --> 08:20.670
<b>Really?</b>

08:21.310 --> 08:22.520
<b>What's she say?</b>

08:23.840 --> 08:27.060
<b>"Dear Libra and Alucia,</b>

08:27.060 --> 08:31.010
<b>"I'm sorry I haven't come to visit.</b>

08:31.010 --> 08:32.390
<b>"I'm doing well.</b>

08:32.820 --> 08:36.100
<b>"I have my own atelier now."</b>

08:36.650 --> 08:40.090
<b><i>I don't know this part...</i></b>

08:40.090 --> 08:43.630
<b>"I've heard the news about you two.</b>

08:43.630 --> 08:46.360
<b>"So you finally got the 
king's permission, huh?</b>

08:47.620 --> 08:51.160
<b>"Congratulations on your marriage!</b>

08:53.550 --> 08:59.560
<b>"I'm giving you both my very best 
floral decoration, with my thanks.</b>

09:00.140 --> 09:05.060
<b>"Libra, Alucia. May every happiness be yours!</b>

09:05.650 --> 09:07.000
<b>"Best wishes, Kris!"</b>

09:17.000 --> 09:20.030
<b><i>This story—it's Kikuchi's story.</i></b>

09:20.890 --> 09:22.330
<b><i>Kris is Kikuchi,</i></b>

09:22.800 --> 09:26.090
<b><i>and my behavior is reflected in Libra.</i></b>

09:27.170 --> 09:29.840
<b><i>If those two didn't wind up together...</i></b>

09:32.690 --> 09:33.540
<b><i>This must be</i></b>

09:34.390 --> 09:36.120
<b><i>Kikuchi's answer.</i></b>

09:39.050 --> 09:41.050
<b>Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki S2</b>

09:42.990 --> 09:47.200
<b><i>Right. I guess that's life 
for you. It's one tough game.</i></b>

09:47.770 --> 09:53.870
<b><i>It's unreasonable; the more 
you try, the harder it gets;</i></b>

09:53.870 --> 09:56.820
<b><i>there are way more things that 
go wrong than go right...</i></b>

09:57.350 --> 10:00.830
<b>But... it's not a garbage game.</b>

10:02.010 --> 10:05.360
<b><i>I'll rest for a bit. And then...</i></b>

10:05.830 --> 10:08.570
<b><i>I'll go back to this game called "life."</i></b>

10:09.350 --> 10:10.510
<b>Tomozaki!</b>

10:16.580 --> 10:17.500
<b>Mimimi...</b>

10:20.630 --> 10:22.020
<b>The play...</b>

10:22.750 --> 10:24.850
<b>Did it mean what I think it means?</b>

10:26.270 --> 10:29.480
<b>Libra is you, and Alucia is Aoi...</b>

10:30.160 --> 10:31.850
<b>and Kris is Kikuchi.</b>

10:32.630 --> 10:37.360
<b>I <i>want</i> to be talking about how great 
it was, how much I enjoyed it.</b>

10:39.110 --> 10:45.870
<b>But that scene at the end—and you and 
Kikuchi avoiding each other afterward...</b>

10:46.620 --> 10:50.190
<b>It's just weird! You both 
worked so hard on it!</b>

10:50.790 --> 10:55.910
<b>It's <i>weird</i> for you two not to be together 
after a huge success like that!</b>

10:57.080 --> 10:59.660
<b>I guess so. I...</b>

11:00.500 --> 11:01.730
<b>She turned me down.</b>

11:12.010 --> 11:13.000
<b>Mimimi...</b>

11:18.530 --> 11:21.030
<b>Kikuchi's in the library!</b>

11:21.030 --> 11:25.780
<b>The play can't be the <i>only </i>
way she gives you her answer!</b>

11:26.190 --> 11:27.540
<b>Brain!</b>

11:27.540 --> 11:30.260
<b>Aren't you the best gamer around?</b>

11:30.260 --> 11:35.790
<b>Then stick with it to the bitter end, 
till you know for <i>sure</i> it's over!</b>

11:40.160 --> 11:41.100
<b>Thanks.</b>

11:42.560 --> 11:43.520
<b>I'll go there now.</b>

12:14.700 --> 12:16.900
<b>Tomozaki...</b>

12:18.160 --> 12:19.030
<b>Listen...</b>

12:19.770 --> 12:20.640
<b>Yes?</b>

12:22.000 --> 12:23.970
<b>About that last scene...</b>

12:24.540 --> 12:26.490
<b>That's how it all turns out, huh?</b>

12:28.470 --> 12:29.850
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

12:30.130 --> 12:32.430
<b>No apology necessary.</b>

12:36.920 --> 12:37.920
<b>That's...</b>

12:39.400 --> 12:41.680
<b>the conclusion I chose.</b>

12:42.850 --> 12:47.790
<b>It's probably not my place to ask why...</b>

12:48.510 --> 12:50.230
<b>but I'd still like to know.</b>

12:51.410 --> 12:54.000
<b>I'd been thinking...</b>

12:54.360 --> 12:57.790
<b>It's true that Kris might like Libra.</b>

12:58.690 --> 13:02.880
<b>She really does feel like she 
wants to be with him forever.</b>

13:03.430 --> 13:05.120
<b>You mean...</b>

13:05.120 --> 13:05.990
<b>But...</b>

13:06.910 --> 13:10.160
<b>Alucia <i>must</i> be with Libra.</b>

13:11.360 --> 13:13.740
<b>Wait—why?</b>

13:14.260 --> 13:20.020
<b>Alucia is clever but empty: a girl 
who's missing the part at her core.</b>

13:21.020 --> 13:27.200
<b>And Libra is awkward but curious: 
a boy with things he wants to do.</b>

13:27.450 --> 13:30.710
<b>They're complete opposites...</b>

13:31.360 --> 13:35.710
<b>which is why they'd make an ideal couple.</b>

13:35.710 --> 13:37.300
<b>"Ideal"...?</b>

13:38.000 --> 13:40.520
<b>What happened to being 
true to yourself instead?</b>

13:41.840 --> 13:44.300
<b>At first I <i>thought</i> it would work.</b>

13:44.900 --> 13:45.730
<b>But...</b>

13:46.720 --> 13:49.220
<b>Sekitomo High School Culture Festival Play 
My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

13:46.970 --> 13:48.740
<b>It turns out I was wrong.</b>

13:49.220 --> 13:57.730
<b>Sekitomo High School Culture Festival Play 
My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

13:49.530 --> 13:53.160
<b>I was satisfied with what 
you told me at first,</b>

13:53.810 --> 13:57.730
<b>that I shouldn't approach life 
itself from an author's viewpoint</b>

13:58.400 --> 14:01.640
<b>and that I should try to face my own emotions</b>

14:01.640 --> 14:04.190
<b>without forcing them to 
fit the world's ideals.</b>

14:05.250 --> 14:06.240
<b>When I did,</b>

14:06.890 --> 14:12.490
<b>the world looked so vivid—like 
the world Libra showed Kris.</b>

14:12.840 --> 14:17.750
<b>I thought, "Wow, Tomozaki really is amazing."</b>

14:17.990 --> 14:18.890
<b>Then...</b>

14:19.470 --> 14:23.240
<b>But that doesn't work for me.</b>

14:25.310 --> 14:27.760
<b>To live according to one's own emotions</b>

14:28.450 --> 14:30.910
<b>in this story we call the world...</b>

14:30.910 --> 14:36.270
<b>It's too selfish with regard to 
how the other characters feel.</b>

14:37.020 --> 14:43.720
<b>So I'm going to rein myself in and 
live in a way I can see as sincere.</b>

14:44.490 --> 14:46.280
<b>That's my conclusion.</b>

14:47.080 --> 14:49.350
<b>Because that's how I want to live.</b>

14:52.550 --> 14:55.790
<b>And yet—I can't forget...</b>

14:55.790 --> 15:00.290
<b>Sekitomo High School Culture Festival Play 
My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

14:56.310 --> 15:00.290
<b>I can't forget the glittering scenery 
and the world all a-sparkle,</b>

15:00.960 --> 15:04.370
<b>like it was in the other ending.</b>

15:05.590 --> 15:08.420
<b>Even though that's just selfish!</b>

15:11.310 --> 15:12.280
<b>We're the same.</b>

15:13.760 --> 15:15.900
<b>Do you remember, Kikuchi?</b>

15:15.900 --> 15:20.660
<b>Until very recently, I'd been 
ignoring the world at large.</b>

15:20.660 --> 15:22.560
<b>I had no interest in ideals.</b>

15:22.860 --> 15:27.260
<b>I lived in freedom, prioritizing 
my desires over anything else.</b>

15:28.280 --> 15:31.670
<b>But then I met a certain magician</b>

15:30.530 --> 15:33.030
<b>Ultimate Goal 
To be as satisfied with offline life as I am</b>

15:31.670 --> 15:35.050
<b>who taught me how to live 
with an ideal in sight.</b>

15:35.530 --> 15:40.310
<b>So I gave it an honest try, 
and started seeing results.</b>

15:40.870 --> 15:45.210
<b>But along the way, I thought: 
This isn't working after all.</b>

15:45.740 --> 15:50.290
<b>Using skills to get by feels 
insincere to me somehow.</b>

15:50.920 --> 15:55.840
<b>But being honest to my 
emotions—<i>that</i> was sincere.</b>

15:56.630 --> 15:59.350
<b>Does that sound familiar?</b>

16:01.310 --> 16:05.860
<b>I started with emotions and 
learned how to aim for an ideal.</b>

16:06.410 --> 16:11.950
<b>You started with an ideal world and 
learned how to be true to your emotions.</b>

16:13.450 --> 16:15.180
<b><i>We're opposites.</i></b>

16:15.990 --> 16:19.830
<b>Sekitomo High School Culture Festival Play 
My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

16:16.940 --> 16:19.830
<b>Do you know what I did?</b>

16:20.560 --> 16:21.750
<b>I embraced both:</b>

16:22.560 --> 16:24.330
<b>ideals <i>and</i> emotions.</b>

16:24.330 --> 16:28.840
<b>All I had to do was make the 
effort to have both at once.</b>

16:29.440 --> 16:32.090
<b>The same goes for you.</b>

16:32.840 --> 16:34.820
<b>For me... too?</b>

16:34.820 --> 16:36.720
<b>You don't have to pick just one.</b>

16:36.720 --> 16:39.720
<b>You can do your honest best to have both.</b>

16:40.510 --> 16:42.240
<b>Simple, right?</b>

16:43.350 --> 16:45.920
<b>But...</b>

16:47.180 --> 16:49.450
<b>I don't know how.</b>

16:50.390 --> 16:53.240
<b>If Libra is meant to be with Alucia,</b>

16:53.240 --> 16:56.750
<b>and I twist that plot just for 
the sake of my own emotions...</b>

16:57.680 --> 16:59.480
<b>Isn't that just selfish?</b>

17:02.990 --> 17:05.840
<b><i>In Kikuchi's version of the world's ideals,</i></b>

17:05.840 --> 17:09.640
<b><i>the two of us aren't meant to be.</i></b>

17:10.410 --> 17:14.640
<b><i>On the other hand, I'm 
pretty sure she likes me.</i></b>

17:15.200 --> 17:18.360
<b><i>She has to make that contradiction work.</i></b>

17:19.310 --> 17:22.310
<b><i>And, yes, as she says,</i></b>

17:22.310 --> 17:29.810
<b><i>it might be tough in the fictional 
world of Kris, Libra, and Alucia.</i></b>

17:30.960 --> 17:34.310
<b><i>But in </i>this<i> world? It's a cinch.</i></b>

17:35.300 --> 17:40.620
<b>I've got it, Kikuchi. There 
<i>is</i> one foolproof method.</b>

17:41.840 --> 17:44.410
<b><i>It was that simple.</i></b>

17:44.930 --> 17:49.080
<b><i>If Kikuchi can't twist how she 
thinks the world should be</i></b>

17:49.080 --> 17:50.800
<b><i>based only on her own emotions...</i></b>

17:54.690 --> 17:58.590
<b>I like you, Kikuchi. I 
want us to be a couple.</b>

18:00.850 --> 18:06.260
<b><i>I, Fumiya Tomozaki, should choose Kikuchi.</i></b>

18:08.100 --> 18:10.490
<b>Remember what you said?</b>

18:10.490 --> 18:11.190
<b>Huh?</b>

18:12.070 --> 18:18.620
<b>Libra and Alucia each have what the 
other lacks, so they belong together.</b>

18:19.360 --> 18:23.580
<b>Don't you think the same 
goes for Libra and Kris?</b>

18:24.140 --> 18:27.990
<b>Fretting over the same things, 
but in opposite order—</b>

18:27.990 --> 18:32.290
<b>and we find that our words gave 
each other a way to move forward.</b>

18:32.840 --> 18:37.840
<b>Even from an author's perspective 
on this story of life,</b>

18:37.840 --> 18:40.890
<b>don't you think this 
relationship is pretty ideal?</b>

18:45.010 --> 18:46.520
<b>You know...</b>

18:47.160 --> 18:49.850
<b>Libra <i>was</i> always good at opening locks.</b>

18:50.740 --> 18:54.270
<b>Uh-huh. And remember what the Popple said:</b>

18:55.400 --> 18:58.780
<b>"Words are magic."</b>

19:03.280 --> 19:06.290
<b>Complete event map (before culture festival) 
Medium Goal: CLEAR! 
Have a girlfriend before starting year 3  
Congratulations!! 
Today's Assignment Next Goal:</b>

19:05.040 --> 19:06.290
<b>Now, then.</b>

19:06.720 --> 19:08.540
<b>First of all: congratulations.</b>

19:08.840 --> 19:11.320
<b>It's all thanks to you.</b>

19:11.320 --> 19:12.790
<b>Me?</b>

19:13.280 --> 19:16.420
<b>I only wanted to prove that I was right.</b>

19:17.540 --> 19:18.900
<b>True enough.</b>

19:18.900 --> 19:20.680
<b>You get it now, right?</b>

19:20.680 --> 19:23.180
<b>Your character change was a big success.</b>

19:23.490 --> 19:24.520
<b>However!</b>

19:24.520 --> 19:26.470
<b>This is no time to relax.</b>

19:26.470 --> 19:27.680
<b>I'm aware.</b>

19:27.680 --> 19:40.950
<b>Ultimate Goal 
To be as satisfied with offline life as I am</b>

19:27.970 --> 19:31.300
<b>You're nowhere near this final goal.</b>

19:31.860 --> 19:36.060
<b>I'll keep dishing out tricky 
assignments, so stay on the ball.</b>

19:37.090 --> 19:40.950
<b>Oh, and I'm sure you remember 
the matching-accessories task.</b>

19:40.950 --> 19:43.450
<b>You never <i>did</i> complete it.</b>

19:44.920 --> 19:49.200
<b>G-Got it. Hit me with your best shot!</b>

19:54.940 --> 19:57.500
<b>I see. So it went well.</b>

19:58.070 --> 20:00.370
<b>Y-Yeah, it did.</b>

20:00.370 --> 20:05.090
<b>That's a top gamer for you. Never say die!</b>

20:07.610 --> 20:10.390
<b>But dang, Brain, you're a <i>player</i>!</b>

20:10.390 --> 20:13.350
<b>I-I'm really not...</b>

20:13.810 --> 20:16.300
<b>Oh, it's fine.</b>

20:16.300 --> 20:21.860
<b>Knowing you, Tomozaki, you thought things 
over really well when it came to me, too.</b>

20:21.860 --> 20:23.160
<b>I get it.</b>

20:23.590 --> 20:24.860
<b>Sorry.</b>

20:25.120 --> 20:30.250
<b>So... Let's just shake it 
off, all right? Both of us!</b>

20:30.250 --> 20:31.140
<b>Okay?</b>

20:31.710 --> 20:32.670
<b>Got it.</b>

20:33.510 --> 20:34.500
<b>But you know...</b>

20:35.390 --> 20:39.330
<b>If you think I'm going to like you 
forever, you've got another thing coming!</b>

20:39.330 --> 20:41.880
<b>You silly Brain!</b>

21:12.910 --> 21:16.670
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

21:13.950 --> 21:16.670
<b>I've finished the novel, too.</b>

21:16.670 --> 21:18.950
<b>I'd love for you to read it.</b>

21:21.260 --> 21:22.300
<b>What's wrong?</b>

21:22.930 --> 21:24.800
<b>Well, um...</b>

21:24.800 --> 21:27.800
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

21:25.280 --> 21:27.800
<b>It's not actually the official version.</b>

21:28.300 --> 21:31.090
<b>It's a story I wrote for myself.</b>

21:31.090 --> 21:32.760
<b>For yourself?</b>

21:33.840 --> 21:40.320
<b>You told me that I can be 
honest with my own emotions.</b>

21:40.320 --> 21:49.320
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

21:40.960 --> 21:47.000
<b>So this isn't about what's best for the 
story world, but what's best for me.</b>

21:47.000 --> 21:49.320
<b>I tried my hand at that 
kind of story instead.</b>

21:49.320 --> 21:53.160
<b><i>Such was our comfortable, mutually 
understanding relationship.</i></b>

21:53.160 --> 21:58.330
<b><i>I didn't think the coziness we felt would 
change at all just because we were dating.</i></b>

21:58.640 --> 22:00.760
<b><i>However...</i></b>

22:01.210 --> 22:04.290
<b>All right. I'll read it later 
and tell you what I think.</b>

22:04.290 --> 22:05.750
<b>No, you can't.</b>

22:07.880 --> 22:11.260
<b>I want to know here and now.</b>

22:11.260 --> 22:13.600
<b>I-I'll wait.</b>

22:13.890 --> 22:15.480
<b>O-Okay...</b>

22:15.480 --> 22:18.480
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

22:16.010 --> 22:17.420
<b>Then, uh...</b>

22:19.180 --> 22:24.950
<b><i>Kikuchi had started being just the 
tiniest bit demanding toward me.</i></b>

22:26.240 --> 22:27.490
<b>This here...</b>

22:28.800 --> 22:29.630
<b>Yes?</b>

22:29.630 --> 22:31.490
<b>Sorry—hang on.</b>

22:31.490 --> 22:33.740
<b>You've completed the accessories task</b>

22:32.060 --> 22:34.780
<b>Hmm? Is something wrong?</b>

22:35.500 --> 22:36.480
<b>It's nothing.</b>

22:38.000 --> 22:49.010
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

22:38.720 --> 22:41.150
<b><i>Though still unaccustomed 
to the outside world,</i></b>

22:41.720 --> 22:48.010
<b><i>Kris felt like she could walk forever and 
ever as long as Libra was by her side.</i></b>

22:52.840 --> 22:56.460
<b>It's a little embarrassing, 
me being a guy and all...</b>

22:56.460 --> 22:57.620
<b>Oh, come on!</b>

22:57.620 --> 23:01.350
<b>I've always wanted to match like this.</b>

23:01.700 --> 23:06.670
<b>Do you remember what the two of 
us saw from way up in the sky?</b>

23:06.670 --> 23:11.360
<b>I'd never seen such a 
splendid world in my life.</b>

23:11.630 --> 23:17.120
<b>Right—and I never knew being 
up there could feel so amazing.</b>

23:17.800 --> 23:23.130
<b>But you know the most important 
thing you taught me?</b>

23:23.810 --> 23:27.510
<b>This world is absolutely full 
of splendor all around us—</b>

23:27.510 --> 23:31.240
<b>and you don't have to fly to see it.</b>

23:32.560 --> 23:34.140
<b>So thank you.</b>

23:36.010 --> 23:38.160
<b>I love you, Libra.</b>
